            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at Quan Ong Tay",
            "review_text": "Philip H\n1 contribution\n1\ncomment\nMar 2024 • Friends\nThrough a friend's recommendation, I came to have dinner here. But I was really disappointed with the service and food here. I ordered 1 mash potato and 1 beef steak. But I was surprised when they set up cups and spoons. and chopsticks. Only when you ask for cutlery do they bring it out. The potato mash is too salty. Beef steak has no sauce, just dipped in green chili salt. The dish that comes with steak is bake potato, which is also too salty, and stir-fried cove beans, like a Vietnamese dish to eat with rice. The way the food is presented is too simple, like it's made at home, not a restaurant, no decor, no decoration at all. When asking the waitress where the sauce is for the steak, she replied that there is no sauce here, the sauce is marinated in the steak. I said this steak is not marinated in any sauce at all, she replied that it is served here. .Steak with green chili salt.... OMG. Then I met a Western chef, I said: I can't eat steak with this green chili salt sauce. This Western friend said that my restaurant serves Fusion style dishes... I still asked if the restaurant had any sauce besides green chili salt. This person said ok..then you came back to the kitchen and brought me 2 types of sauce: 1 teriyaki, 1 HP sauce.At least I got this sauce.. ok.But when I ate it, oh my god....sauce Take it from the refrigerator and do not reheat it. It's surprising for a restaurant that claims to sell Western food. When I called the waitress, I wanted to order a mixed green side salad but the waitress said she didn't have any. Regarding Steak quality, it is considered okay compared to the price. Above are just a few comments for the restaurant. Just a comment, not a complaint. I hope the restaurant changes a little to be called Basic of a shop or restaurant. The location and restaurant are beautiful, but unfortunately the quality of the food and service is not very good. We also need to train the service people to understand how to serve European dishes. I am also in the FB industry and hope you guys will change and improve. A better way to welcome more and more out-of-province guests to BD in general and the restaurant in particular. Wishing the restaurant business more and more success.\nRead more\nShow original\nWritten March 26, 2024",
