            "review_title": "Review at Quan Ong Tay",
            "review_text": "Martin P\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam37 contributions\n0\nNice place, prices are good but food is very avarage\nJan 2020 • Couples\nWent here for dinner with my wife.\nChicken wings, ribeyes and shrimp.\nSauce on the chicken wings was really good, ribeye was cooked to rare as ordered, but flavor and side dishes were very avarage, didn't blow me away, I must admit. Kinda felt like local chefs let loose trying to do western food that they don't enjoy eating them self.\nShrimp was tasty and there was a generous portion of them, again the sides were underwhelming.\n\nWas really missing some sauce, like a pepper sauce or bearnaise. Only chili lime (I think it was) was available, and that doesn't go well with steak in my opinion. \n\nThe place is nice and comfortable seating, staff were very noisy and goofing around.\n\nSaw they had a wood fired pizza oven so might come back and try that :)\nRead more\nWritten January 6, 2020",
